import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 294 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Forced Level-Up for Plot","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 294 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Forced Level-Up for Plot","no":294,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Plot Kidnaps Setting","Forced Level-Up","Law-First Axiom","Combat Collapse"],"related":["97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0294_模块2-遮天-剧情绑架设定案例.md","filePath":"en/0294_模块2-遮天-剧情绑架设定案例.md"}'),s={name:"en/0294_模块2-遮天-剧情绑架设定案例.md"};function a(r,e,l,h,d,c){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-294-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-cases-of-plot-kidnapping-setting-typical-cases-of-forced-level-up-for-plot" tabindex="-1">Entry 294 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Forced Level-Up for Plot <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-294-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-cases-of-plot-kidnapping-setting-typical-cases-of-forced-level-up-for-plot" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 294 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Forced Level-Up for Plot&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 7) | Benchmark base: Documents 97, 14, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-rules-are-meant-to-be-broken-—-but-only-when-the-protagonist-needs" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Rules are meant to be broken — but only when the protagonist needs <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-rules-are-meant-to-be-broken-—-but-only-when-the-protagonist-needs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Rules are meant to be broken — but only when the protagonist needs&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> expressly states &quot;plot must not kidnap setting.&quot; This entry uses Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; concrete cases to dissect the operating mechanism of &quot;plot kidnaps setting,&quot; a chronic long-web-novel disease. Laws can be expanded, but expansion must go through the &quot;legislative procedure,&quot; not the &quot;protagonist&#39;s rage&quot; procedure. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Energy waste caused by plot kidnapping:</p><ul><li>To let the protagonist &quot;just barely win,&quot; villain strength is temporarily adjusted; narrative tension distorts</li><li>Readers learn &quot;anyway the protagonist will turn it around&quot;; suspense mechanism fails, emotional investment wasted</li><li>Supporting characters forcibly dumbed down or fed XP to衬托 the protagonist; supporting-character narrative energy wasted in vain</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Regression plot kidnapping creates inside the world-view:</p><ol><li><strong>Strong-one ranking arbitrary</strong>: who is strong or weak depends not on cultivation logic, but on who this scene needs to win</li><li><strong>Rule authority collapses</strong>: the world&#39;s physical laws (cultivation system) are proven modifiable at will; this world no longer feels &quot;real&quot;</li><li><strong>Historical weight imbalanced</strong>: important supporting characters&#39; sacrifices only serve protagonist emotion; civilization history degrades to the protagonist&#39;s backdrop</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Plot kidnaps setting is essentially predation on setting-authority:</p><ul><li><strong>Protagonist immunity</strong>: Ye Fan always breaks through, comprehends, lucks out at critical moments; this is &quot;protagonist-exclusive setting-modification authority&quot;</li><li><strong>Supporting characters instrumentalized</strong>: supporting characters&#39; meaning is to feed the protagonist XP, intelligence, emotion; their cultivation logic is cut at will</li><li><strong>Enemies staircased</strong>: enemy strength always one notch above / one notch below the protagonist, only to let the protagonist &quot;just barely win&quot;; the world becomes a training ground revolving around the protagonist</li></ul><p>Plot kidnapping setting also has a hidden consequence: it makes the world lose &quot;self-running&quot; ability. A healthy world-view should be: even if the protagonist is absent some day, the world still runs by rules; supporting characters still have their own reasons to act. But Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; world, once Ye Fan does not participate, supporting characters&#39; behavioral logic immediately blurs — they do not know what to do, only wait for Ye Fan to push. This shows Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; world was never an independently running world, but a stage revolving around the protagonist. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Myriad Races republican design is precisely to let every supporting character, every race have their own goals, interests, action logic — the protagonist is one member, not the world&#39;s engine.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Shrouding&#39;s Plot Kidnapping</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Law-First</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Protagonist comprehends and breaks through at any time</td><td>Breakthrough has law thresholds, all equally applied</td></tr><tr><td>Villain strength fluctuates with plot</td><td>Combat power law-anchored by realm, calculable</td></tr><tr><td>Supporting characters sacrificed for emotion</td><td>Supporting characters are also Myriad Races republican members, with complete fates</td></tr><tr><td>Rules step aside for the protagonist</td><td>Law-anchored authority benefits all beings, no one can bypass</td></tr><tr><td>World revolves around the protagonist</td><td>Myriad Races co-build, world does not revolve around any one person</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: mark all chapter nodes in Shrouding-the-Heavens where the &quot;protagonist cross-tiers at critical moments&quot;</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: count the frequency of these cross-tier events and their correlation with &quot;plot climaxes&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: if the protagonist cannot cross-tier, which plot will not hold</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; roughly half of climax plot depends on &quot;plot kidnaps setting&quot; to hold, verifying kidnapping is structural, not occasional</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. The protagonist&#39;s critical-moment comprehension, lucking-out, cross-tier frequency is too high</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. Plot kidnapping is retconning&#39;s direct precursor</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: medium</strong>. The kidnapping&#39;s beneficiaries are precisely Ye Fan and his peer oligarchs</li></ul><p>Plot kidnapping setting also produces a special kind of reader fatigue: readers no longer look forward to &quot;how the protagonist wins by wisdom and rules,&quot; but to &quot;how the protagonist turns it around this time.&quot; When the turnaround itself becomes expectation, victory loses weight. Why Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; late battles feel &quot;empty&quot; is precisely because readers know Ye Fan will definitely win, definitely have a way; so the battle process is no longer suspense, just procedure. Heng Yuan Zhou requires the protagonist to win within the law framework — victory is calculable, costly, truly requires applying rules — not by the author temporarily modifying rules.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: suspense fails, supporting characters instrumentalized, emotion distorted</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: predating setting-modification authority, predating supporting characters&#39; fates</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: the Tang-Luo world&#39;s protagonist leveling also has a halo, but not to the &quot;rules step aside at any time&quot; degree</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: supporting characters, foreign races, ancients are all plot tools, no independent personality</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: a kidnapped world-view cannot serve as a cross-plane baseline</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Changing rules for the thrill&quot; is the cheapest thrill. The true hard-core is: rules are there, the protagonist still wins — because he obeys and skillfully uses rules, not because he makes rules kneel to him.</p><p>Plot kidnapping setting&#39;s final cost is making the author lose reverence for his own world. When the author feels rules can serve himself, he no longer respects this world; and an author who does not respect his own world cannot make readers respect this world.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · plot kidnaps setting cases described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./292_模块2-遮天-境界膨胀批判.html">Entry 292 · Realm Inflation</a> · <a href="./293_模块2-遮天-吃书烂尾深度分析.html">Entry 293 · Retcon / Bad Ending</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/97-设定矛盾自查表.html">97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const g=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
